[strategy/guidance/application/responsive-layout/GUID-APP-UI-002-responsive-layout-implementation-guidance.md#1-mobile-first-utility-application]

### 1. Mobile-First Utility Application

Write base styles for mobile, then apply breakpoint prefixes to override at larger viewports:

```tsx
// ✅ Mobile-first — single column on mobile, two columns at md, three at lg
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
  {items.map((item) => (
    <Card key={item.id} {...item} />
  ))}
</div>

// ❌ AVOID — desktop-first (requires overriding at smaller viewports)
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 xs:grid-cols-1">
  {/* never shrink classes with Tailwind — always grow from the base */}
</div>
```

